# GetMasterBrokerStatus — return the master's own MQTT-broker connection
# state. Operator diagnostics for "is the master itself online?"
#
# **Why this exists**: an FMS operator needs to distinguish a per-AGV
# connection problem (one AGV's last-will fired) from the master itself
# losing its broker (no orders can flow to ANY AGV). GetDeviceStatus
# answers the per-AGV question; this service answers the master-broker
# question.
#
# Pairs with the on_broker_disconnected / on_broker_reconnected virtuals
# on VDA5050Master and the BrokerStatusSnapshot exposed via
# get_broker_status() (Task #70).
#
# Request takes no fields — there is one master-broker connection per
# master process.
---
# True iff the master is currently connected to its broker. Distinct
# from per-AGV connection state in GetDeviceStatus.
bool connected

# Wall-clock time at which the master last observed a broker
# disconnect. Zero (epoch) if no disconnect has occurred since the
# master process started.
builtin_interfaces/Time last_disconnect_at

# Number of times the master's broker connection has been
# (re)established since the process started. Initial successful
# connect counts as 1; each Paho-driven auto-reconnect increments by 1.
# A value of 0 means the master has never successfully connected.
uint64 reconnect_count
